                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5f7532a5-7f03-43de-890a-60671dd37521",
                        "source_entry_id": "db2fa093-3bfa-3106-9f5e-38f6246c0e2d",
                        "source_sense_id": "6143eb83-87ac-3cb1-b563-125f9052d875",
                        "target_lang_word": "ellipsoid",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ellipsoid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25862615-67a1-3037-bb15-bf70d2ce350a",
                                        "entry_id": "f11cde16-87ee-3c8d-9ec3-c9bbe60d08b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surface, all of whose cross sections are elliptic or circular (including the sphere), that generalises the ellipse and in Cartesian coordinates (x, y, z) is a quadric with equation x²/a² + y²/b² + z²/c² = 1."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4d3e6d8-6fdf-4ce9-83e0-7bd07b2ee74f",
                                                "sense_id": "25862615-67a1-3037-bb15-bf70d2ce350a",
                                                "text": "Polarizability can be imagined as a three-dimensional ellipsoid centred on the centre of the molecule, as shown in Figure 10.4."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "410bd48a-50a3-442e-ac5c-0b715b79fa33",
                                                "sense_id": "25862615-67a1-3037-bb15-bf70d2ce350a",
                                                "text": "Because only ellipsoids of rotation have been adopted in practical geodesy and surveying and triaxial ellipsoids have been limited to theoretical studies, we will use the term ellipsoid for brevity to mean ellipsoid of rotation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65d549fe-1353-4385-893e-6e621d521729",
                                                "sense_id": "25862615-67a1-3037-bb15-bf70d2ce350a",
                                                "text": "As mentioned before, modern geodetic datums rely on the surfaces of geocentric ellipsoids to approximate the surface of the earth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "770c4468-dd19-34c6-b4fc-94e5b1b3aa25",
                                        "entry_id": "f11cde16-87ee-3c8d-9ec3-c9bbe60d08b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Such a surface used as a model of the shape of the earth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e35e52f7-778c-4729-aec3-5c6c8169a1e5",
                                                "sense_id": "770c4468-dd19-34c6-b4fc-94e5b1b3aa25",
                                                "text": "Here the geoid is thirty meters below the ellipsoid."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ellipsoid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f786707-9a06-3c69-a241-3758dd9f7a13",
                                        "entry_id": "5db6f314-cffb-3169-8816-13753da33144",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Shaped like an ellipse; elliptical."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69bffc4d-d464-3bae-a6ae-0f215171c61e",
                                        "entry_id": "5db6f314-cffb-3169-8816-13753da33144",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to an ellipse; elliptic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76e86cb6-f9c1-3495-8f72-e66c2c0f8070",
                                        "entry_id": "5db6f314-cffb-3169-8816-13753da33144",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having the tridimensional shape of an ellipse rotated on its long axis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "583a0b7b-3c03-4f85-9213-577a5b6d67a3",
                        "source_entry_id": "db2fa093-3bfa-3106-9f5e-38f6246c0e2d",
                        "source_sense_id": "6143eb83-87ac-3cb1-b563-125f9052d875",
                        "target_lang_word": "elliptical",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "elliptical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bda4b93e-f645-3fa3-8a71-73301f270c08",
                                        "entry_id": "6516d8ec-c732-3817-92d9-9a6ae617f988",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a shape of, or reminding of, an ellipse; oval."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0900d16-2a15-4ee5-a253-570bf551877a",
                                                "sense_id": "bda4b93e-f645-3fa3-8a71-73301f270c08",
                                                "text": "Having admitted that the projectile was describing an orbit around the moon, this orbit must necessarily be elliptical; science proves that it must be so."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3fe94c1-230b-3f1a-a4f8-718b0cda1645",
                                        "entry_id": "6516d8ec-c732-3817-92d9-9a6ae617f988",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, or showing ellipsis; having a word or words omitted."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06fd6dd6-d34f-4e1d-acb5-67a317ad18e7",
                                                "sense_id": "b3fe94c1-230b-3f1a-a4f8-718b0cda1645",
                                                "text": "If he is sometimes elliptical and obscure, it is because he has so much to tell us."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66c30ba1-407d-3cd2-888d-04d1dc9481b6",
                                        "entry_id": "6516d8ec-c732-3817-92d9-9a6ae617f988",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Concise, condensed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of speech"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff50e4ad-9ccb-4051-a3ab-2507009b0a6c",
                                                "sense_id": "66c30ba1-407d-3cd2-888d-04d1dc9481b6",
                                                "text": "Browning's dark and elliptical mode of speech, like his love of the grotesque, was simply a characteristic of his, a trick of his temperament, and had little or nothing to do with whether what he was expressing was profound or superficial."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60759061-c906-4c9f-9d22-6f66c352b96b",
                                                "sense_id": "66c30ba1-407d-3cd2-888d-04d1dc9481b6",
                                                "text": "He was called a tramp; but that was only an elliptical way of saying that he was a philosopher, an artist, a traveller, a naturalist and a discoverer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "acf6628c-5a97-382e-bf17-8422b60af4fc",
                                        "entry_id": "6516d8ec-c732-3817-92d9-9a6ae617f988",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Elliptic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "elliptical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bda845d6-0e74-3657-83a3-f8047bb01716",
                                        "entry_id": "70dce56e-4760-308a-beeb-5f0de8bed7f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An elliptical galaxy."
